---
import DocLayout from "../../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<DocLayout
  title="Hosted quickstart"
  description="Connect to hosted rob-mcp over Streamable HTTP or JSON, begin with free discovery, and understand the Base Sepolia x402 test flow."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p><h1>Connect to hosted rob-mcp</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Keep the deployment configurable. These examples use <code>$ROB_MCP_URL</code> rather than inventing
    a production host.
  </p>
  <h2>Set the service URL</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`export ROB_MCP_URL="https://your-deployment.example"`}
    label="Hosted endpoint"
  />
  <h2>Start with free discovery</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`curl --fail-with-body \\
  -X POST "$ROB_MCP_URL/api/v1/tools/list_stock_tokens" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  --data '{"search":"AAPL","chain":4663}'`}
    label="Free JSON call"
  />
  <h2>Connect hosted MCP</h2>
  <p>
    The Streamable HTTP endpoint is <code>$ROB_MCP_URL/mcp</code>. Use an MCP client with x402
    payment support for paid tools; structured outputs use the same schemas as the JSON API.
  </p>
  <h2>Test payment safely</h2>
  <p>
    Use Base Sepolia and a throwaway funded test wallet. The first paid request receives 402 with <code
      >PAYMENT-REQUIRED</code
    >; an x402-aware client creates an EIP-3009 authorization and retries with <code
      >PAYMENT-SIGNATURE</code
    >.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    Base mainnet availability is not implied. Paid mainnet redistribution remains gated by O-5.
  </div>
</DocLayout>
